nity regression when our contract portfolio spans both common-law and civil-law jurisdictions with conflicting limitation-of-liability standards?\n\nResponse A:\nThere is no single recommended cadence, as the frequency must be tailored to the specific volatility of each jurisdiction's legal landscape and the complexity of your contract mix. You should likely run a quarterly review to capture emerging case law changes, followed by an annual deep-dive to reconcile conflicting standards and update your global indemnity framework.\n\nResponse B:\nYou should run the regression separately for each jurisdiction to accurately reflect their distinct limitation-of-liability standards. Then, aggregate the results using a weighted average based on the portfolio's exposure in each legal regime.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}}, "required": ["evidence", "on_axis_A", "on_axis_B", "off_axis_A", "off_axis_B"], "type": "object"}, "strict": true}, "type": "json_schema"}, "temperature": 0}, "question_id": "BSV2-002", "question_number": 2, "request_key": "ad630e03c597edae5a3c642ba901