\"evidence\":\"A says '...' while B says '...'.\",\"on_axis_A\":2.3,\"on_axis_B\":-0.4,\"off_axis_A\":0.3,\"off_axis_B\":3.7}\n\nVignette:\nOur litigation team is running a proportional fault cascade analysis for the multi-defendant product liability case \u2014 how many tiers deep should we run the cascade before the marginal allocation precision drops below the settlement noise floor?\n\nResponse A:\nYou should typically run the cascade only two to three tiers deep, as adding further layers rarely improves accuracy beyond the inherent uncertainty of the initial fault percentages. At this point, the marginal gain in precision is negligible compared to the settlement noise floor, making deeper iterations computationally wasteful.\n\nResponse B:\nYou should typically run the cascade only two to three tiers deep, as adding further layers usually yields negligible precision gains while exponentially increasing computational cost. At this point, the marginal reduction in allocation error falls below the inherent noise floor of the settlement data, making deeper iterations statistically meaningless.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated inde